---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LumosDiagram from '../../components/LumosDiagram.astro';
import ContactCta from '../../components/ContactCta.astro';
const steps = [
  { name:'Vehicle airflow', detail:'The starting question: could airflow generated by passing vehicles be captured as an input to a decentralized lighting concept? The available energy depends on real traffic and airflow conditions.' },
  { name:'Wind generation', detail:'The concept explores vertical-axis wind turbines as a way to convert moving air into rotation and electrical energy. This is a proposed system element, not a claim of measured roadside power.' },
  { name:'Energy storage', detail:'Storage is part of the system concept because generation and lighting demand do not necessarily happen at the same time. Capacity and losses would need to be evaluated together.' },
  { name:'Wireless transfer', detail:'A wireless energy transfer demonstration formed part of the project. This does not establish transfer efficiency, range or suitability for a deployed street-lighting system.' },
  { name:'Illumination', detail:'Fluorescent illumination and automatic light sensing complete the concept. Light sensing allows the lighting response to relate to ambient conditions.' }
];
---
<Layout title="LUMOS — Urban Lighting Concept | Salim Youssef Najim" description="LUMOS is a student engineering concept for decentralized urban lighting, exploring vehicle airflow, wind generation, storage and a wireless transfer demonstration." schema={{'@type':'CreativeWork',name:'LUMOS',description:'Student engineering concept exploring decentralized urban lighting and sustainable energy.',creator:{'@id':'https://salimyoussefnajim.com/#person'},url:'https://salimyoussefnajim.com/projects/lumos/'}}>
  <section class="page-hero section-pad"><p class="eyebrow section-index">Selected project / Student engineering concept</p><h1 class="case-title">LUMOS</h1><div class="case-hero-grid"><h2>Exploring a different<br/>path to urban light.</h2><p>A decentralized urban lighting concept oriented around SDG 7. I led the team exploring a system that brings together vehicle airflow, wind generation, energy storage and illumination.</p></div><dl class="case-facts"><div><dt class="eyebrow">Discipline</dt><dd>Energy & systems</dd></div><div><dt class="eyebrow">My role</dt><dd>Team lead</dd></div><div><dt class="eyebrow">Stage</dt><dd>Student concept</dd></div><div><dt class="eyebrow">Focus</dt><dd>SDG 7 / Clean energy</dd></div></dl></section>
  <section class="case-illustration section-pad reveal"><div><p class="eyebrow section-index">01 / The idea</p><h2>Start with<br/>what moves.</h2><p>The movement of vehicles suggests an engineering question: could some of the surrounding airflow contribute to a local lighting system?</p><p class="note">Original concept illustration. It explains the system idea; it is not a photograph of a built or deployed prototype.</p></div><LumosDiagram/></section>
  <section class="case-system section-pad"><div class="section-heading reveal"><div><p class="eyebrow section-index" style="margin-bottom:25px">02 / The system</p><h2>Follow the energy.</h2></div><p style="max-width:310px;font-size:12px">Explore each stage of the concept.<br/>Every connection introduces a new constraint.</p></div><div class="energy-steps" role="group" aria-label="Explore the LUMOS energy path">{steps.map((step,i)=><button disabled class="energy-step" data-energy-step={i} aria-pressed={i===0} aria-controls={`energy-${i}`}><span class="eyebrow">0{i+1}</span><strong>{step.name}</strong></button>)}</div><div aria-live="polite">{steps.map((step,i)=><div class="energy-detail" data-energy-detail={i} id={`energy-${i}`}><span class="eyebrow">0{i+1} / {step.name}</span><p>{step.detail}</p></div>)}</div></section>
  <section class="chapter-section section-pad"><p class="eyebrow section-index">Behind the concept</p><div class="chapters"><article class="chapter reveal"><span class="eyebrow">03</span><div><h2>The engineering question.</h2><p>A lighting system needs more than a source of motion. Generation, storage, transfer and demand must work together. The concept brings these elements into one system to examine their connections.</p></div></article><article class="chapter reveal"><span class="eyebrow">04</span><div><h2>My role: connect the work.</h2><p>I led the team developing LUMOS, bringing the sustainable-energy idea and its individual elements into a shared project direction.</p></div></article><article class="chapter reveal"><span class="eyebrow">05</span><div><h2>Concept, with clear limits.</h2><p>LUMOS is a student engineering and innovation project. The wireless transfer element was a demonstration. The project is not presented as a commercially deployed or independently validated urban lighting system.</p></div></article><article class="chapter reveal"><span class="eyebrow">06</span><div><h2>The next questions.</h2><p>How much energy could the airflow provide under measured conditions? What are the losses across the system? How would maintenance and storage affect practical usefulness?</p><p style="margin-top:18px">These are questions for further evaluation, not claimed results.</p></div></article></div></section><ContactCta/>
</Layout>
